{"name":"Kiln Fired","hex":"#da7631","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kiln","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An oven or furnace or a heated chamber, for the purpose of hardening, burning, calcining or drying anything; for example, firing ceramics, curing or preserving tobacco, or drying grain."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bake in a kiln; to fire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiln"},{"term":"fired","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["dismissed, terminated from employment.","Heated in a furnace, kiln, etc., to become permanently hardened."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of fire"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fired"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kiln","blocks":[{"text":"A kiln is a thermally insulated chamber, a type of oven, that produces temperatures sufficient to complete some process, such as hardening, drying, or chemical changes. Kilns have been used for millennia to turn objects made from clay into pottery, tiles and bricks. Various industries use rotary kilns for pyroprocessing and to transform many other materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG/330px-Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiln","wikidata":"Q1724341"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG/500px-Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG/500px-Charcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charcoal kiln in California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharcoal_Kilns%2C_California.JPG"},{"srcset":